page ref_template {
  title = "Lab file: template and source"
  chapter_header "Lab file: template and source" {
    kicker       = "Reference · reference"
    reading_time = "9 min read"
    updated      = "2026-09-02"
    version      = "vmlab 0.9"
  }

  p <<DOC
    This chapter is the field-by-field reference for the `template {}` block
    and its required `source {}` child. A template block describes how to
    build a sealed base image for the store; [Templates and the store](guide_templates)
    explains the build flow and [vmlab template](cmd_template) the verbs that
    run it. Template blocks live at the top level of a `vmlab.wcl`, beside a
    `lab {}` or in a file of their own with no lab at all. `vmlab template
    build` reads `./vmlab.wcl` unless `--file` names another.
  DOC

  h2 "template {}"
  p <<DOC
    One buildable template. The build creates a working disk from the
    `source`, boots it with the hardware declared here, runs the provisions
    and playbooks, shuts the VM down and seals the disk into the store under
    `<arch>/<name>/<version>/`. The hardware fields are recorded in the
    template's metadata and become the inheritance layer for every VM cloned
    from it.
  DOC
  code wcl { source = <<'SRC'
template "<name>" {
  arch        = "x86_64"
  version     = "24.04"
  registry    = "ghcr.io/owner/ubuntu-24.04"
  profile     = "linux-modern"
  cpus        = 2
  memory      = 4GiB
  disk        = 20GiB
  display     = "virtio-vga"
  cpu_model   = "pentium3"
  accel       = "tcg"
  firmware    = "ovmf"
  tpm         = false
  secure_boot = false
  nested      = false
  gui         = false
  qemu_args   = []
  first_boot  = "scripts/first-boot.ws"
  agent       = true
  source "…"  { … }
  gpu         { … }
  media       { … }
  provision "…" { … }
  playbook "…"  { … }
  nic         { … }
  disk "…"    { … }
  variant "…" { … }
}
SRC
  }
  table {
    rows:
      | "Field" | "Type" | "Default" | "Meaning" |
      | "`name`" | "utf8 (label)" | "required" | "Template name, for example `linux-modern`; the inline block label." |
      | "`arch`" | "utf8" | "required" | "Architecture. Selects the QEMU system emulator." |
      | "`version`" | "utf8" | "required" | "Version string, non-empty. Name, arch and version together are unique." |
      | "`registry`" | "utf8" | "none" | "Full OCI repository to publish to and to version-bump against." |
      | "`profile`" | "utf8" | "none" | "Guest OS profile supplying hardware defaults for the build VM." |
      | "`cpus`" | "i64" | "from profile" | "vCPU count for the build VM. Inherited by clones." |
      | "`memory`" | "ByteSize" | "from profile" | "RAM for the build VM, for example `8GiB`. Inherited by clones." |
      | "`disk`" | "ByteSize" | "from source" | "Working disk size for the build, for example `64GiB`. Required for a `scratch` source." |
      | "`display`" | "utf8" | "from profile" | "QEMU display device string for the build VM." |
      | "`cpu_model`" | "utf8" | "from profile" | "QEMU `-cpu` model for the build VM, for example `pentium3`, replacing the accelerator default. Inherited by clones. Cannot be combined with `nested = true`." |
      | "`accel`" | "utf8" | "from profile" | "Accelerator for the build VM: `kvm` or `tcg`. Inherited by clones. `tcg` cannot be combined with `nested = true`." |
      | "`firmware`" | "utf8" | "from profile" | "Firmware: `ovmf` or `seabios`." |
      | "`tpm`" | "bool" | "from profile" | "Enable a TPM 2.0 device." |
      | "`secure_boot`" | "bool" | "from profile" | "Enable secure boot; OVMF only." |
      | "`nested`" | "bool" | "`false`" | "Enable nested virtualisation for the build VM." |
      | "`gui`" | "bool" | "`false`" | "Watch the build VM in a VNC viewer." |
      | "`qemu_args`" | "list<utf8>" | "none" | "Raw QEMU flags for the build VM. The escape hatch." |
      | "`first_boot`" | "utf8" | "none" | "wscript run on the first instantiation of a clone, before it turns ready." |
      | "`agent`" | "bool" | "`true`" | "Bake the vmlab-agent service into the image." |
      | "`source {}`" | "child" | "required" | "What the build starts from. Exactly one of four forms." |
      | "`gpu {}`" | "child" | "none" | "GPU acceleration for the build VM only: passthrough, virgl or vulkan, with an optional `host_gpu`. Never recorded for clones." |
      | "`media {}`" | "children" | "none" | "ISO or floppy images attached to the build." |
      | "`provision {}`" | "children" | "none" | "Provision scripts that drive the build." |
      | "`playbook {}`" | "children" | "none" | "config-weave playbooks applied to the build VM, interleaved with provisions in declaration order. Steps stream as structured build progress." |
      | "`nic {}`" | "children" | "none" | "NICs for the build VM. Optional; the build VM may be air-gapped." |
      | "`disk {}`" | "children" | "none" | "Additional disks attached during the build." |
      | "`variant {}`" | "children" | "none" | "Sealed variants built on the base after it seals, each its own disk state. See the variant {} section below." |
  }
  p <<DOC
    `media`, `provision`, `playbook`, `nic`, `disk` and `gpu` are the same
    blocks a `vm` carries; see [vm and its children](ref_vm).
  DOC
  h3 "The build VM's GPU"
  p <<DOC
    A `gpu {}` on a template or a variant gives the **build VM** a GPU and
    nothing else. Validation checks it as a lab VM's, `passthrough`
    included. At the build boot the lab daemon picks the host GPU as it does
    for a lab VM: the `host_gpu` named, or the host's default, with its
    render node, the Vulkan loader filter, the PCI-filter layer and the host
    config's `qemu_binary` and `qemu_env`. A `host_gpu` this host does not
    declare warns and falls back to the default. The build log names the
    pick as `host_gpu=<name>`, and the build VM's `qemu.log` header shows
    the argv and environment it produced.
  DOC
  p <<DOC
    The block is never recorded in the template's metadata: a clone's GPU is
    the lab's choice, so a clone that declares no `gpu {}` boots on the
    profile's plain display. Use it when an install only completes on a
    working paravirtual GPU, such as a Windows GPU driver package that
    verifies its kernel driver started, and leave `display` alone.
  DOC
  h3 "Versions and the registry"
  p <<DOC
    The declared `version` is a fixed prefix naming the upstream identity,
    such as an OS release. Each build appends a counter: the stored version is
    `<version>.<N>`, where N is one higher than the highest existing build
    with that prefix, or 0 for the first. When `registry` is set the existing
    builds are read from its tags, so the counter continues across machines;
    otherwise the local store decides. Changing the prefix restarts the
    counter at `.0`. `vmlab template build --version` pins an explicit
    version instead. `registry` is also the repository `vmlab template push`
    publishes to; see [Distributing templates over registries](guide_registries).
  DOC
  h3 "The first-boot script and the agent"
  p <<DOC
    `first_boot` is read at build time and baked into the template's
    metadata, so a clone runs it on its first start without the lab needing
    the file. It runs before the VM turns ready. With `agent = true` the
    build waits for the guest-installed agent's handshake before sealing and
    records the agent version in the metadata. With `agent = false`, or on a
    profile with no agent channel, the check is skipped and the build log
    says so.
  DOC
  h3 "Validation"
  list {
    li "`arch` is one of the known architectures: `x86_64`, `x86`, `aarch64`, `riscv64`, `loongarch64`, `s390x`, `ppc64`."
    li "`version` is non-empty, and no other template in the file has the same arch, name and version."
    li "`profile`, if set, names a known profile."
    li "A `scratch` source requires `disk`."
    li "`first_boot` and every `provision` script exist under the template's root and compile."
    li "A `playbook` on a template whose `arch` is not `x86_64` is rejected."
    li "Every `media` and `disk` source folder exists."
    li "Variant names match `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}`, are not `base`, and do not repeat; exactly one variant sets `default = true`, unless there is only one."
  }
  code wcl {
    filename    = "examples/templates/ubuntu-24.04/vmlab.wcl"
    source_file = "../../examples/templates/ubuntu-24.04/vmlab.wcl"
  }

  h2 "source {}"
  p <<DOC
    What the build starts from. The inline label is the kind, and the kind
    decides which fields apply. Exactly one `source {}` per template; the
    schema rejects a template without one.
  DOC
  code wcl { source = <<'SRC'
source "iso"      { path = "./installer.iso" }
source "iso"      { url = "https://…/installer.iso" sha256 = "…" }
source "qcow2"    { path = "./base.qcow2" }
source "template" { from = "x86_64/ubuntu-24.04@24.04.4" }
source "scratch"  { }
SRC
  }
  table {
    rows:
      | "Field" | "Type" | "Default" | "Meaning" |
      | "`kind`" | "utf8 (label)" | "required" | "Source kind: `iso`, `qcow2`, `template` or `scratch`; the inline label." |
      | "`path`" | "utf8" | "none" | "Local file path, for `iso` and `qcow2`. Mutually exclusive with `url`." |
      | "`url`" | "utf8" | "none" | "Remote artefact URL, for `iso` and `qcow2`. Requires `sha256`." |
      | "`sha256`" | "utf8" | "none" | "SHA-256 of the remote artefact. Required with `url`." |
      | "`from`" | "utf8" | "none" | "Source template `<arch>/<name>[@<version>][#<variant>]`, for kind `template`: a layered build. No `#` seeds from the default variant, `#base` from the base." |
  }
  p "The four kinds:"
  list {
    li "**`iso`**: an installer ISO. The build boots it with the attached media and lets the provision script drive the installer. A remote artefact is downloaded to the cache and verified against `sha256` before use."
    li "**`qcow2`**: an existing disk image, imported as the base."
    li "**`template`**: a layered build. An existing store template is the base, more provisioning runs, and the result seals as a new template. `from` must be a local store reference; a registry reference or `scratch` is rejected here. On a source with variants, no `#` seeds from its default variant, `#<variant>` from that variant, and `#base` from its base; the build boot runs the first-boot script of what was selected, and none for `#base`. The selected disk and everything beneath it are flattened into the working disk."
    li "**`scratch`**: a blank disk of the template's `disk` size. The attached installer media and provision script do everything."
  }
  p <<DOC
    Validation requires exactly one of `path` and `url` for `iso` and
    `qcow2`, `sha256` whenever `url` is set, a `path` file that exists, and a
    `from` template that is in the store. An unknown kind is rejected.
  DOC

  h2 "variant {}"
  p <<DOC
    One variant of the template: a named, sealed disk state built on the
    base by booting an overlay on it and running the variant's own steps. A
    template with variants is referenced as `<arch>/<name>#<variant>`, and
    a reference without `#` selects the default variant; see
    [Templates and the store](guide_templates). The motivating case is
    Windows: the base is installed and updated but not generalized, and each
    variant generalizes after its own changes.
  DOC
  code wcl { source = <<'SRC'
template "windows-11" {
  …base build: source, provisions ending in a clean shutdown, no sysprep…
  first_boot = "scripts/firstboot.ws"

  variant "standard" {
    default = true
    provision "scripts/generalize.ws" { }
  }
  variant "win3d" {
    description = "GPU driver installed"
    secure_boot = false
    gpu { mode = "vulkan" }          // the build VM only; host_gpu = "AMD1" to pin
    provision "scripts/win3d-setup.ws" { }
    provision "scripts/generalize.ws" { }
  }
}
SRC
  }
  table {
    rows:
      | "Field" | "Type" | "Default" | "Meaning" |
      | "`name`" | "utf8 (label)" | "required" | "Variant name, `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}`. `base` is reserved." |
      | "`default`" | "bool" | "see meaning" | "The variant a reference with no `#` selects. Exactly one variant sets it, unless there is only one." |
      | "`description`" | "utf8" | "none" | "One line saying what the variant is for, shown by `vmlab template list`." |
      | "`first_boot`" | "utf8" | "the template's" | "wscript run on the first instantiation of a clone of this variant, before it turns ready." |
      | "`profile`" | "utf8" | "the base's" | "Guest OS profile for this variant." |
      | "`cpus`" | "i64" | "the base's" | "vCPU count." |
      | "`memory`" | "ByteSize" | "the base's" | "RAM, for example `8GiB`." |
      | "`display`" | "utf8" | "the base's" | "QEMU display device string." |
      | "`cpu_model`" | "utf8" | "the base's" | "QEMU `-cpu` model." |
      | "`accel`" | "utf8" | "the base's" | "Accelerator: `kvm` or `tcg`." |
      | "`firmware`" | "utf8" | "the base's" | "Firmware: `ovmf` or `seabios`." |
      | "`tpm`" | "bool" | "the base's" | "Enable a TPM 2.0 device." |
      | "`secure_boot`" | "bool" | "the base's" | "Enable secure boot; OVMF only." |
      | "`qemu_args`" | "list<utf8>" | "the template's" | "Raw QEMU flags for the variant's build VM, replacing the template's." |
      | "`gpu {}`" | "child" | "the template's" | "GPU acceleration for the variant's build VM only, replacing the template's. Never recorded for clones; see the build VM's GPU above." |
      | "`media {}`" | "children" | "none" | "ISO or floppy images attached to the variant's build. The template's own media stay with the base build." |
      | "`provision {}`" | "children" | "none" | "Provision scripts the variant's build runs, interleaved with its playbooks in declaration order." |
      | "`playbook {}`" | "children" | "none" | "config-weave playbooks applied to the variant's build VM." |
      | "`nic {}`" | "children" | "the template's" | "NICs for the variant's build VM, replacing the template's when any are declared." |
  }
  p <<DOC
    The hardware fields override what the base recorded, field by field, for
    the variant's build boot and for every clone of the variant; a field the
    variant leaves out follows the base. `secure_boot = false` on a variant
    of a Secure Boot base boots its build, and its clones, on the firmware
    without Secure Boot. `gpu {}` is the exception: it reaches the variant's
    build boot and never its clones.
  DOC
  h3 "How a variant builds"
  p <<DOC
    `vmlab template build` seals the base first. On a template with
    variants the base embeds no first-boot script: the template's
    `first_boot` is each variant's to inherit, and a variant's own
    `first_boot` replaces it. Then each variant builds, the default first and
    the rest in file order. A variant build creates an overlay on the sealed
    base, boots it on the variant's hardware, waits for the agent, runs the
    variant's provisions and playbooks, and shuts down gracefully. It runs
    **no first-boot script**: the base was never generalized, so there is
    nothing to specialize until a clone of the finished variant starts. The
    overlay is then pointed at its base by the relative path
    `../../disk.qcow2`, hashed, and installed with its metadata under the
    store lock.
  DOC
  p <<DOC
    A failed variant stops the build; the base and every variant installed
    before it stay installed, and nothing of the failed one is left behind.
    `vmlab template build <name> --variant <v>` builds or rebuilds just that
    variant onto the installed version. A rebuild is refused while a
    machine's clone is backed by the variant: destroy those machines first.
  DOC
}
